    "description": "In this video, Chef John shows you how to make Irish beer cheese puffs. He uses Irish butter, Irish beer (stout), and Irish cheddar to create these snacks. He adds some salt, sugar, and all-purpose flour to the melted butter and beer mixture in a saucepan. Once the dough starts to form, he stirs in two large eggs one at a time, followed by a sharp Irish cheddar and a couple of shakes of cayenne. After transferring portions of the dough to a Silpat-lined baking sheet, Chef John tops them with more grated cheddar and places them in the oven. The result is easy-to-make cheesy snacks that are perfect for any party or gathering.",
